ested":true,"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":0.111429,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.120118,"nucleus_score":-2.02094,"pct_ad":0.28303,"pct_control":0.296698,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.999342,"donor_log2fc":-0.110184,"donor_lfcse":0.0738658,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-2.10795e-05},{"cell_type":"Oli","gene_symbol":"ANAPC7","gene_symbol_current":"ANAPC7","gene_id":"ENSG00000196510","nucleus_tested":true,"nucleus_significant":false,"nucleus_direction":"lower in AD","nucleus_padj":0.40197,"nucleus_log2fc":-0.0197181,"nucleus_score":-0.928995,"pct_ad":0.223374,"pct_control":0.225891,"donor_test":"not significant","donor_padj":0.896442,"donor_log2fc":-0.048875,"donor_lfcse":0.063674,"donor_log2fc_shrunk":-0.0114789}],"modules":[],"degas_bulk_de":false,"drug_target":false}},"description":[{"gene_id":"ENSG00000196510","entrez_id":["51434"],"uniprot":["Q9UJX3"],"ncbi_summary":"This gene encodes a tetratricopeptide repeat containing component of the anaphase promoting complex/cyclosome (APC/C), a large E3 ubiquitin ligase that controls cell cycle progression by targeting a number of cell cycle regulators such as B-type cyclins for 26S proteasome-mediated degradation through ubiquitination. The encoded protein is required for proper protein ubiquitination function of APC/C and for the interaction of APC/C with certain transcription coactivators. Multiple transcript variants encoding different isoforms have been found for this gene. [provided by RefSeq, Nov 2008].","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q9UJX3","text":"Component of the anaphase promoting complex/cyclosome (APC/C), a cell cycle-regulated E3 ubiquitin ligase that controls progression through the cell cycle (PubMed:18485873, PubMed:27120157, PubMed:27509861). APC/C acts by mediating ubiquitination and subsequent degradation of target proteins: it mainly mediates the formation of 'Lys-11'-linked polyubiquitin chains and, to a lower extent, the formation of 'Lys-48'- and 'Lys-63'-linked polyubiquitin chains (PubMed:18485873). APC/C catalyzes assembly of branched 'Lys-11'-/'Lys-48'-linked branched ubiquitin chains on target proteins (PubMed:29033132). APC/C is activated by CDC20 in the metaphase/anaphase transition of cell cycle, targeting the degradation of cyclin B and securin (PubMed:27120157, PubMed:27509861). APC/C is regulated by the mitotic checkpoint complex (MCC), which inhibits APC/C and delays chromosome segregation (PubMed:27509861). Has an enzyme-substrate adapter activity mediating the processive ubiquitination of specific substrates (PubMed:34942119). Involved in brain development through the specific ubiquitination and clearance of MKI67 from constitutive heterochromatin after neuronal progenitors exit mitosis (PubMed:34942119)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[],"alphafold_accessions":[]}